Post 9: DevSecOps Engineer Interview 
Intermediate Level (2–4 Years)
At this stage, security isn’t an add-on — it’s embedded into every pipeline by design! 🛡️ 
With 2–4 years of experience, DevSecOps engineers focus on security automation, threat modeling, and compliance in fast-paced DevOps environments.
Ready to test your security automation expertise? 👇
💡 Common DevSecOps Interview Questions (2–4 Years Experience): 
1️⃣ How do you integrate SAST, DAST, and SCA tools into CI/CD pipelines? 
2️⃣ Explain IaC security scanning using tools such as Checkov or Terrascan. 
3️⃣ How do you manage secret scanning and rotation in production environments? 
4️⃣ What’s your approach to container security (image scanning, runtime protection, sigstore)? 
5️⃣ How do you conduct threat modeling for microservices-based systems? 
6️⃣ Describe how you generate and manage an SBOM (Software Bill of Materials). 
7️⃣ How do you secure Kubernetes clusters (RBAC, Network Policies, Pod Security Standards)? 
8️⃣ What’s your plan for compliance as code (SOC2, PCI-DSS, HIPAA automation)? 
9️⃣ How do you prioritize vulnerabilities using CVSS scores and exploitability? 
🔟 Explain how you’d implement Zero Trust in a cloud-native DevOps setup.
🎯 Pro Tip: 
Strong DevSecOps practitioners automate policy enforcement — for instance, replacing manual security checks with CI/CD gates that cut review time by 80%. 
Balance security with speed: “We caught 95% of vulnerabilities pre-merge — without slowing down deployments.” ⚡
